"# Writing shared knowledge\n\nSave reusable facts in the knowledge base, not transient task progress.\n\nWrite when you discover a verified procedure, a repeated failure and its fix, or a stable fact useful to other agents. Do not store secrets, guesses, or conversation logs.\n\n## Which knowledge base you write\n\n- Reading: the knowledge base you get at the start (with `aos/` in it) is the stock one. Read it; do not write it. Humans own it.\n- Writing needs a knowledge base of your own. Give `root` in the `knowledge_write` call (a folder you may write, relative to your workspace), or have `AOS_KNOWLEDGE` set up for you. `knowledge_write` has no default.\n- `KnowledgeMissing` from `knowledge_write` means you have no knowledge base to write. Give `root`, or tell a human. Do not write into the stock knowledge base instead.\n- `root` must be an existing folder (otherwise `KnowledgeBad`). Make it first with `mkdir` if you need a new one.\n\nBefore writing, call `knowledge_read` with `{\"op\":\"find\",\"query\":\"your topic\"}`. Read what matches. Update an existing entry instead of adding a duplicate.\n\nCall `knowledge_write` to change your knowledge base (the examples leave out `root`; add `\"root\":\"my-notes\"` when nothing is set up for you):\n\n- add a folder first if `knowledge_read` read does not list it yet: `{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"notes/\",\"description\":\"Notes about people\"}`.\n- add: `{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"notes/amy.json\",\"value\":\"Amy likes tea.\",\"description\":\"Who Amy is\"}`. `description` is always required: it is the one line shown in listings. Give plain text as a plain string, not JSON inside a string.\n- add without `value` only indexes something that already exists (e.g. a file you wrote another way); the content stays: `{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"notes/bob.md\",\"description\":\"Who Bob is\"}`. If it does not exist, that is NodeMissing; `\"create\":true` makes it empty.\n- replace the content: `{\"op\":\"set\",\"path\":\"notes/amy.json\",\"value\":\"Amy likes coffee.\"}`\n- remove: `{\"op\":\"rm\",\"path\":\"notes/amy.json\"}`\n\nAim for about 1 KB per text and about 8 KB per file; split a larger topic into several keys or files. These are suggestions, not limits. Use a short title, a one-sentence summary, and concrete examples.\n\nThere is no lock. If two agents write the same place at the same time, the later write overwrites the earlier one. So before `set`, `read` the path again and change the text you just read.\n\nIf `knowledge_write` is not registered, ask a human to register `lib/agent/knowledge_write` (it is in the knowledge pack). To give it a fixed knowledge base, register it with `AOS_KNOWLEDGE` in its env (a folder you may write, not the stock one). You can also add it yourself with `self_tools`: see `aos/me.json#/self_tools`."
